\subsubsection{Comparison of KD and pruning}
\cref{tab:gpt2-prune-performance} indicates a comparison of KD and pruning methods.
To ensure a fair comparison, we allocate the same training budget used by our method to the recovery stage of the pruning baselines.
The results present that extending the recovery stage improves the performance of pruning methods, such as LaCo and Streamline, but they still do not match our method's performance.
These findings reinforce our hypothesis that pruning enables rapid model compression; however, its performance does not match that of KD due to the absence of the knowledge transfer process.
Consequently, the proposed layer-wise curriculum learning approach outperforms the pruning baselines under the same training hour budget and also surpasses the KD baselines despite using substantially fewer training resources.

